<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.7.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING - SetupRun takes the method that writes a line, output.WriteLine, instead of xunit's ITestOutputHelper; Core no longer depends on xunit. BREAKING - an assertion on a variable that was never set now fails, and EnsureRanToCompletion now also fails for a step that never ran, naming why, so a run cancelled between stages no longer passes. The blocking PersistentEnvironmentContext constructors and OnRequirementResolved are removed; use CreateAsync and EnvironmentResources.Required. BREAKING - no public member takes an optional parameter any more, so 1.x can grow without breaking compiled packages: framework exceptions take (message[, inner]) with RecoverySteps and AvailableOptions as init properties; steps declare IO with contract.Input/Output/InputArtifact/OutputArtifact; debugger signals take DebugRunStart, DebugEntityTransition and DebugValueUpdate; RunContext.Detached takes DetachedContextOptions; polling returns SequentialPollingResult.Done/NotYet; Offers takes ValueTraits; DeclaredResource and the component-graph records use init properties. Five exception types nothing threw are deleted. A run's live state now answers to one gate: the IsFrozen properties on the stores, artifacts and resource values and the public ArtifactWriteTicket are gone, every channel refuses a finished run with the same message, and an abandoned attempt can no longer record effective settings or open run state. New: RunRecord&lt;T&gt;, a package's own run-scoped record under the same rules, and ArtifactStore.Assign, so a setup records what it created - a key the database assigned - under the same gate. SetupArtifact now declares its reference's variables when the run is planned, so one nothing writes is refused before the run starts. New: VariableStore.SetSecretVariable, for a credential a step reads into a variable - the run uses it and every description of it says (secret). New: EnvComponent.StateOf, for a component to read what a declared dependency produced in this run.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Core's own suite, and nobody else. A grant to another package's suite is the same private
		     handshake as a grant to the package: whatever that suite may reach for, every other package's
		     suite may not - and it hides that a surface is missing. Config's suite never used one, and
		     Simple's hand-built the run's pieces until RunContext.Detached existed to hand them over. -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
